\textbf{2.2 Main technical result}

We consider a quantum oracle algorithm \emph{A} as formalized above, and
we define a two-stage algorithm \emph{S} with black-box access to
\emph{A} as follows. In the first stage, \emph{S} tries to predict
\emph{A}'s future output \emph{x}, and then, upon input a (random)
\emph{Θ}, in the second stage tries to output what \emph{A} is supposed
to output, but now with respect to \emph{Θ} instead of
\emph{H}(\emph{x}).
\end{quote}

