\begin{quote}
\textbf{4} \textbf{Application to Fiat-Shamir signatures}
\end{quote}

Any Fiat-Shamir non-interactive proof system can easily be transformed
into a public-key signature scheme.15

The signer simply proves knowledge of a witness (the secret key) for a
composite statement \emph{x∗}:= \emph{x∥m}, which includes the public
key \emph{x} as well as the message \emph{m}. The signature \emph{σ}
then consists of a proof for \emph{x∗}.

\textbf{Definition 18} \emph{A binary relation R with instance generator
G is said to be} hard \emph{if for any quantum}

\begin{quote}
\emph{polynomial-time algorithm A we have}
\end{quote}

Pr {[}(\emph{x, w′}) \emph{∈R} : (\emph{x, w}) \emph{←G,
w′←A}(\emph{x}){]} \emph{≤µ}(\emph{η})

\begin{quote}
\emph{for some negligible function µ}(\emph{η})\emph{, where G is such
that it always outputs a pair} (\emph{x, w}) \emph{∈R.}
\end{quote}

\textbf{Definition 19} \emph{A} Fiat-Shamir signature scheme \emph{based
on a} Σ\emph{-protocol} Σ = (\emph{P, V}) \emph{for a hard relation R
with instance generator G, denoted by} Sig{[}Σ{]} \emph{is defined by
the triple (Gen, Sign, Verify), with}

\begin{quote}
\textbf{--} Gen\emph{: Pick} (\emph{x, w}) \emph{←G, set sk} :=
(\emph{x, w}) \emph{and pk} := \emph{x.}\textbf{--}
Sign\emph{H}(\emph{sk, m})\emph{: Return} (\emph{m, σ}) \emph{where σ
←PH F S}(\emph{x∥m, w})\emph{.}\textbf{--} Verify\emph{H}(\emph{pk, m,
σ})\emph{: Return VH F S}(\emph{x∥m, σ})\emph{.}

\emph{Here} (\emph{PH F S, V H F S}) = FS{[}Σ\emph{∗}{]}\emph{, where}
Σ\emph{∗}= (\emph{P∗, V∗}) \emph{is the} Σ\emph{-protocol obtained from}
Σ \emph{by setting P∗}(\emph{x∥m}) = \emph{P}(\emph{x}) \emph{and
V∗}(\emph{x∥m}) = \emph{V}(\emph{x}) \emph{for any m.}

Note that by definition of FS in Section 3.2, we use \emph{VH}

We investigate the following standard security notions for signature
schemes. \emph{F S}(\emph{x∥m, σ}) as shortcut for \emph{V} (\emph{x∥m,
a, H}(\emph{x∥m, a})\emph{, z}).

\textbf{Definition 20 (}sEUF\emph{−}CMA\emph{/}EUF\emph{−}NMA\textbf{)}
\emph{A signature scheme fulfills} strong existential unforgeability
un-der chosen-message attack (sEUF\emph{−}CMA) \emph{if for all quantum
