\multicolumn{20}{@{}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 38\tabcolsep) * \real{1.0000} + 38\tabcolsep}@{}}{%
The following is a generalization of Lemma 7 from {[}Unr12{]}. It
relates the success probability of applying a random projection to a
state vector with the success probability of sequentially applying
\emph{t} random projections, where ``success probability'' here is in
terms of the (average) square-norm of the projected state vector. This
statement gives us the means to relate the probability of a interactive
prover making the verifier accept with the probability of an extractor
making the verifier accept \emph{t} times, when rewinding \emph{t −}1
times and using a freshly random (and independent) challenge each
time.} \\
